Priya (AE): Quick sync — Orchid Health wants a short POC. Requirements: streaming chat with function/tool calls to their appointment API, strict JSON schema for final output, SAML SSO, and customer-managed KMS. SLA expectation: ~200ms tail for interactive flows. Traffic: bursty, peak ~1k qps. Pricing ask: rough hosted vs Dedicated reserved commit for ~10M tokens/month. They also handed over a security questionnaire (SOC2 + KMS/HSM questions). Can someone own tech answers + a compact SDK streaming + function_call example we can share in the repo?

Ben (Solutions): I can own the SDK sample + runbook. Quick clarifier: strict schema means we should server-side validate and reject malformed results, right? And for tool calls they want synchronous webhook calls (our runtime invokes their endpoint and waits for a response) rather than async fire-and-forget?

Priya (AE): Correct. Validate final shape server-side and return a single JSON object. Tool calls are synchronous webhooks to Orchid's API.

Ben (Solutions): Got it. I'll create a minimal Node example showing streaming SSE + a final function_call event with args. Will include a tiny express verification endpoint for signatures. Pseudo-snippet we'll include in README:

Ben (Solutions): ```js
// pseudo Redwood streaming flow
const stream = client.chat.stream({ model: 'redwood-lowlatency', messages, functions, stream: true });
for await (const ev of stream) {
  if (ev.type === 'partial') process.stdout.write(ev.delta);
  if (ev.type === 'function_call') {
    // synchronous POST to customer webhook
    await fetch(customerWebhook, {method: 'POST', body: ev.args});
  }
  if (ev.type === 'final') validateAndEmit(ev.json);
}
```

Ben (Solutions): I'll also add schema unit tests and a demo harness that simulates webhook latencies so Orchid can see retry behavior.

Tom (SRE): KMS & SSO notes: for customer-managed KMS we recommend Dedicated or Private. Hosted supports envelope encryption but not full KMS key separation for audit. For SAML we have a standard IdP metadata exchange + handshake runbook. I'll sanitize and drop the public-safe runtime excerpt into the POC repo.

Tom (SRE): I'll attach a checklist: IP allowlist, egress ranges, TLS cert expectations, and a short note on our signature verification scheme.

Jess (Product): On latency: to hit ~200ms tail we should recommend a low-latency model variant (quantized), enable KV/prefix caching between turns, and keep interactive batching disabled or minimal. I'll produce an Optimize profile with recommended params (batch size, latency targets, quantization profile).

Ellen (Sales Eng): Pricing preview: Hosted is fastest to start. For steady 10M tokens/month a Dedicated reserved commit (3–12mo) usually reduces unit cost by ~15–30% depending on GPU class. I'll run a concrete comparison (hosted vs Dedicated small/medium/large commit) and include an appendix for HSM costs. ETA EOD.

Priya (AE): Action items assigned: Ben -> sample repo + README + tests; Tom -> public-safe KMS/SAML answers + checklist; Jess -> latency config and Optimize suggestions; Ellen -> hosted vs Dedicated cost sheet. I'll schedule a 30m review tomorrow. Owning: Priya.

